    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The full test suite (a single `AcceptanceTest` in this project) passes with `BUILD SUCCESS`.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe spec requires the owner response to expose `checkDigit` \u2014 a single Luhn check digit computed over the digits of the `customerCode`. This is a derived, read-only field, so I followed the same pattern as the existing derived fields (`membershipNumber`, `membershipLevel`, etc.):\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a `checkDigit` property to the Owner schema (`type: integer`, `format: int32`, range 0\u20139, `readOnly`). The OpenAPI generator produces the getter/setter on `OwnerDto` from this.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added `@Mapping(target = \"checkDigit\", expression = \"java(toCheckDigit(owner))\")` and a `toCheckDigit(Owner)` default method implementing the standard Luhn check-digit algorithm over the digits in `customerCode`, returning `null` when the customer code is absent (mirroring `toMembershipNumber`).\n\nThe acceptance test recomputes Luhn from the returned `customerCode` and asserts the exact digit \u2014 it now passes.",
